From: Analog Rytm MKII research
Subject: [PATCH] target/m68k: do not decode MAC-with-load as dual accumulate

EMAC_B dual-accumulation instructions use the no-load opcode form.  The
existing condition instead selects load-form MAC instructions whenever the
low extension bits are nonzero, then applies an unintended second
accumulation.

diff --git a/target/m68k/translate.c b/target/m68k/translate.c
--- a/target/m68k/translate.c
+++ b/target/m68k/translate.c
@@ -5437,7 +5437,7 @@ DISAS_INSN(mac)
 
     ext = read_im16(env, s);
 
     acc = ((insn >> 7) & 1) | ((ext >> 3) & 2);
-    dual = ((insn & 0x30) != 0 && (ext & 3) != 0);
+    dual = ((insn & 0x30) == 0 && (ext & 3) != 0);
     if (dual && !m68k_feature(s->env, M68K_FEATURE_CF_EMAC_B)) {
         disas_undef(env, s, insn);
         return;
